{
  "contract": "ori-specs/firmware-commands/v2.md#signing-domains",
  "version": 2,
  "comment": "Golden vectors for the signing domains of firmware-commands/v2. A device must accept every case in 'cases' and refuse every case in 'reject_cases' as bad_signature, persisting nothing, evaluated against its verifier_context; a runtime signer must reproduce each accepted case's command, preimage and wire bytes. Each cross_purpose entry holds the runtime key's signatures over one object in the command domain, in the liveness domain and alone: they differ, and each verifies over its own preimage only. Signed with the TEST-ONLY runtime and rogue seeds of the liveness corpora; never use them in production.",
